// Title: Python Function Execution Security Warning Disabled In Excel
// Sigma ID: 023c654f-8f16-44d9-bb2b-00ff36a62af9
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: @Kostastsale
// Date: 2023-08-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects changes to the registry value "PythonFunctionWarnings" that would prevent any warnings
//   or alerts from showing when Python functions are about to be executed. Threat actors could run
//   malicious code through the new Microsoft Excel feature that allows Python to run within the
//   spreadsheet.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/data-security-and-python-in-excel-33cc88a4-4a87-485e-9ff9-f35958278327
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_registry_office_disable_python_security_warnings.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Microsoft\\Office\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Excel\\Security" and ProcessCommandLine contains "PythonFunctionWarnings") and ProcessCommandLine contains " 0"
